   457	Cael went out and came on him under the eave, in what was left of the light. He had a rag in his hand, and he was rubbing a hand's breadth of the tarred oak clean, beside the left-hand post. When it was done to his liking he took a tack from between his teeth and pressed it into the wood there, with nothing under it.
