   459	"What's coming?" said Cael.
   460	
   461	"Paper. I had it by word of mouth at noon, from a carter off the north-west." Pike stood back and looked at his tack, twice. "A hold's slip. It'll be on the oak by morning."
   462	
   463	"Which hold?"
   464	
   465	"None you've heard of. It's got a ford."
   466	
   467	"I've had enough of fords," said Lira, from the door.
   468	
   469	Pike put the rag in his belt.
   470	
   471	"It's on the oak in the morning," he said. "Read it before you say so."

