   291	*No.*
   292	
   293	She knew what a second one was. She had sat in a loft and heard it laid out with a charred stick. *Never two at once.* A burst would crack over that bay like the first, and thirty animals that were running from one loud thing would have another to run from, and it would be going off beside the only shelter on the mountain. She had been the loud thing once this morning without being asked. She would not be it a second time by choice.
   294	
