   305	She had watched those points go down in barns and annexes and on the end wall of a whitewashed room, a dozen at a time, each no bigger than a barley grain. She had seen them joined in threes, and once, at a sitting, sixteen. She had never seen a road. It stood up across the whole face above the rock, two straight burning lines that met in a point high on the slope, as wide as a street and as long as a field; and the animals coming down on it split like a log under a wedge.
