Movement 3’s extra length is earned. The traverse does more than stage the collapse: it turns each person’s old trained habit into useful work, then tests the difference between derived knowledge and proof. Oryn’s arrival also preserves the book’s key boundary—she reads broken bone but cannot read Cael, and she does not turn that failure into a label.
