   129	Karis slept. She woke to eat, and to ask which day it was and write the number down, and then she folded herself up again between two boxes with Seln's coat over her and was gone. Cael watched her do it and was easier each time. On the mountain she had looked at her own hands before she looked at anything else, and by the third morning on this road she had stopped.
