   274	
   275	She put no question to herself about what he was. She had heard a small pale person say, by a lantern, that there was a thing she would not write down; she had seen a calfskin with rings on it, and heard a quiet man say *yet*. Those were other people's trades. She had gone into that loft with one thing that she knew, and she had said it, and come down a ladder.
   276	
