editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:26:- **Costs on the page:** Brom's forearm open to the bone, wrist to mid-arm; Lira's right ankle, bound flat; Karis's palms cut to the meat, unable to hold a pen; Cael's calf bitten through, in and out, felt only when the water went cold. "Four… Out of five." The bowman: "none of you shouted." **The seal log** (protected; the only restatement). Pike's line by carter; "First honest number…"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:29:- **Lowmarch, day 60:** fourteen slips. Seln reads the board and takes the well: "I keep waiting for someone to ask for my report." **Brom at the plank's end:** "What does the board pay a man with no Path at all." / "Same as anyone… What'd he do?" He writes it on an old slip and keeps it against his skin, the second time in his life (Rooke was the first). Pike: "Held a dog with a shoulder and a river, that one." **The mail** sorted aloud. Hesk's letter (protected), and the grandmother he did not know about. The log. **The saying** at the book, the sheet rewritten by hand: twelfth. "Teague's still eleven up. He'll speak to you when you've cost him something."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:23:- **The hour's mending at the line by lantern:** "There. Back." (she does not mention the clock). The state, said because a thing not said is not a finding. **The order (protected, exact)** and the sling; "One arm. From here to the snow."; "The ankle's a tape and a season…"; Oryn flat on the road. Karis's written lines. Seln: "Nothing." Brom: "Hand." / "Morning. Wash it. I've nothing tonight." The log, including **the Book 9 plant line, exactly.** Close: "It worked in there." / "Yours." / "Yes." / "Later." / "Later."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:24:- **The camp at the stone (night of the 96th → dawn of the 98th):** the unfiled entry (protected). Morning arithmetic aloud: Karis's throat ("Days. Hoarse before it's anything."); Brom's hand ("String… That's two."); **Cael's calf read and not mended**, the fourth failure ("I don't say a finding four times to a patient and change it on the fifth."). Oryn against the stake: "Three in two days… That's a route." The route's far end, eleven days north. **Seln at the stake**: the charcoal circle from memory lies on the carter's circle; "Ignorance doesn't stamp iron."; "The Compact knows what quiet ground does. And it's filed somewhere we can't reach." (once); "No… I carried the maps. I never saw the file." Karis: *Where*, then *Entered as said*, then *Blank. Stamped. Filed.* **The contract re-read:** a question, not a recovery; "We just told them."; "Six is wrong. I'm a stop." / "They'll write six." The dead hound dragged off and the bolt cut out (five in the sleeve); rations in sixths; nobody says *yours*. Second-night log. **Dawn of the 98th: Oryn's eight crossings alone.** He watches and does not write it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:26:- **The loft council, without her:** the conditions as he built them (sustained; stakes on both sides; earnest, on him and not against him); Karis's torn sentence (protected); the price; Lira: "Then tell her. Tonight. Before."; his argument, and its honest underside ("the real one is that I don't know what she'd say"); Seln's "nearest thing to it… I'd enter both."; Brom's "What's it cost her?". **The covenant written before** (protected, whole).
