editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/compiled-prompt.md:1926:- **The table, as staged after repair:** he lies still for the telling and for her naming of it; he gets down for what it did and what it costs, and stands by the table for about a quarter of an hour; she gives him his book, tells him to lie down again (the protected line), puts the horn cup in his hand, takes the book back, and sits on the stool with it for a minute before she sends him out.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/compiled-prompt.md:1929:- **The listening (flag):** his own current at the edge of every thought, quick and slow; the nine by sound (Wind, dry grass going over; the read, a millstone through a floor; Ember, a wick ticking; Pressure, a bellows; Compression, hemp under load; Anchor, one held note; Blade, a wet finger on a glass; Shadow, a hush that drops the others; Storm, a sea turning over). It cannot be refused, since it asks for nothing. Three nights. Asked on the 101st where it is loudest, he answers at the breastbone: it is not louder there, it is nearer (the protected line).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/compiled-prompt.md:1946:- **Oryn's lateness (flag):** nine late at Thornwater and eleven at the next on the 104th (meaning to go on the 106th); she stays to read the arm at the fortnight; "sixteen out of this gate… A round never gives a day back; it takes one." (the 110th, in the yard); "Oxhollow's seventeen days late and the old woman's knee doesn't care what's under a floor" (the loft, the protected line), and in her window the odd day is the old woman's knee and Oxhollow is the 121st. Her window: the child was last heard on the 89th, looked for on the 109th, and cannot be heard before the 126th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/compiled-prompt.md:1974:**Pike's book and the wall.** **Eight lines**: the eighth is the protected Fallow line, entered on the 101st and sent up on bark (read aloud at the hold's board by Brom, and answered as not wrong); Pike has not said it in the crew's hearing. The wall's order after it is not known to the crew. The two HOLD slips are unresolved on the page. The broker's clerk's copy went west on the boat of the 102nd.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/compiled-prompt.md:1993:- **Oryn:** day 112 closes just short of the mill; she is sixteen late out of Thornwater and seventeen late at Oxhollow, has left the mule, and has not forgiven Cael or received the self-reading (`manuscript/chapter-44.md:223–301`). Her exact location on day 113 is Millrace under M7, subject to the protected north conflict (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:30`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/compiled-prompt.md:1995:**Movement 6 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Same-author repair r1: the fourteen audit fixes kept and their joins smoothed (Cael's "Then it's owed, and I've heard you say so." before Oryn's restored unit; Karis asks Oryn for a healer's count at the next edge and is not answered; Lira's "And if it's sooner than Thornwater?"); seven tracked passages restaged, ch40 scene 4 re-entered (Gault's line comes back as Brom reads Pike's bark aloud; Hesk's parcel found missing at the cleared board); ch41 now runs forward in time; the research run states its observed-versus-supposed thesis once, at the count on the night of the 103rd. Sol recheck r1: **CLOSE**, no line fixes: every brief item and all seven tracked passages resolved; the telling keeps Oryn's full agency with no retroactive consent or forgiveness; the Movement 7 joins promise neither a sixth place nor a joining. Gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected / 42 protected. 37597 words. Author-sourced sections above refreshed from the post-repair report.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/compiled-prompt.md:2008:- **#50:** Seln's "Six years I've wanted a face" stands verbatim and unglossed; the case's twelve years appears only in his window. **#51:** "Tomorrow makes three" is not explained. **"The still place"** is not said.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/compiled-prompt.md:2012:All reads on Sol (gpt-5.6-sol): editorial, cold read, source-distance (3 tracked passages, all in ch52; one dense scene), plan / canon / protected-text audit (ten line fixes applied by the coordinator, including the five protected units the author had left as markers and the replacement of the invented groove staging). Same-author repair r1 in progress when this block was written; the CLOSED note follows when the recheck returns.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:22:- **The telling on the table** from the beginning: fourteen, eleven seconds, a training floor, the count. Sources by Path, not by name, except the three she has had her hands on. The notice said aloud. The page fetched from the loft and read twice in its counted places. **Her answer** (protected): "So I couldn't read you because…" … "Then use it on yourself first. Before anyone… I want to be the one you tell." Nobody has ever attached a condition to the mechanism before, and she is right to. "You're the colour of the wall…"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:25:- **The birthday (day 102):** Lira instigates one-armed, pays one-handed, and has been practising the pouch for a week without saying so. Brom acquires three kinds ("Three."). Six places in the common room. Oryn at the table "like a woman who has sat at a great many tables and stayed at none of them." **The line written** (protected). "A stop. Good. Write it down before it changes." **Pike's Fallow copy** by carter; "Six went in. Six came out." beside Gault's last note. Hesk's package does not come, and the absence sits at the table unremarked. Seln: "He's counted her… So has the broker." The apples argument, which Karis loses on the merits.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:26:- **The first self-reading** that night, alone, as she set it. Ten flows and no banks (a limit of the reading, written above everything else). Then **the place session nine logged**: not a current, not the tenth, not any of the nine; near the middle, where everything is nearer; the ten go *round* it. Three things he can count. It is **not named**: no "still place" yet. The inventory, and **the three words retired with the reason** (protected). "Hundred and two in hand; six to the hold for the room and the kid."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:27:- **The week of tables (days 103–109).** The ring laid flat (eleven sheets cut to the uprights' heights); the tally of *kinds* she will not number from one site. **Five findings, each a scene:** (1) *the Quieting*: grammar for a process, not a place; (2) **identical failure** across five sigils (Iron R1, Copper, no ranking, Bronze, Iron R4; Lira's clock in Lira's words), and the looms sentence, unfiled (protected); Seln's "Six… I'm counting it." and the struck six; (3) **the strata as a physical demonstration** (four chips oldest to the right; the knife marked and the floor didn't; no stroke, no join, no laid edge; weathering past the founding stone), with **[UNBOUND] once** (protected), then Brom's "Say it with less."; (4) **the stakes, once, in four sentences**; (5) **the observation entered and the interpretation stopped**: "It's a fear." / "Does it help?" / "It's just correct." Oryn works the hold in the yard (nine late here, eleven at the next) and looks at the table once.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:30:- **Day 110.** Lira first at the gate-walk at dusk, in the order he has had for fifteen days (protected exchange); the fighter's question ("It felt like a Third-day."); her hand along the plank to his boot; "Then six." **The circle of six**: what each of the four saw, in order; Karis's five findings said; Seln's "Yet."; Oryn's "I'm not going to guess past it."; nobody puts a verb between the facts; the four wheres; "We find the others…"; "One at a time, for money." Oryn: "North in the morning… Don't go in without me…"; her hand on Seln's shoulder. **Brom at the ladder** ("It's a count. You like counts."). **The Vastin window** (three sentences). **Oryn at the well**: the rule written while she watches (protected); "Once is a morning" (the debt's terms set by her: three readings on different days, then all of it at once); "Don't read anyone on the road to find out whether you can."; the note written under the rule. **The second pole** in the log (protected).
