editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-04.md:295:It was a dry stream cut deep through red earth, twelve feet down and thirty across at the bottom, with banks too steep to stand on. The road went into it by a ramp dug out of the eastern side and climbed out by another on the west. A trickle ran in the bed, no wider than a hand. Karis looked at that trickle before she looked at anything else, and went down and drove a peeled stick into the gravel at its edge, and cut a notch in the stick at the waterline with her knife.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-04.md:299:The woman with the hides was on the western lip with her two mules. She had got a third of her load up the ramp by herself, a bale at a time, and she was grey to the hair with dust. Cael knew her, for she had once laid a barley cake on the shaft of their cart, and she had been standing ten feet away when an old man asked him what he was. She pointed at the bed of the wash with her whole hand, and that was her greeting.
