+### Movement 8 — chapters 54–60
+
+- Calendar holds: Hall entry day 119 (54:3–15; 55:153–165); three readings completed and telling on day 120 (55:169–219, 295–301); four-site argument/departure day 121 (57:91–149); Oryn turns north day 122 (58:3–63); return begins day 124, first snow and Lowmarch day 129 (59:3–15, 47–49, 121–139); last ferry day 130 (60:47–95); Oryn's letter arrives day 131 (60:219–225).
+- Hall adds a new rule and a new cost rather than replaying the Ring/Stair: its blind organism hunts weight that stays, abandons its round once it has a target, and can be diverted by a deliberately harder Anchor (53:229–339; 54:91–107, 159–187). The rescue uses ordinary learned movement, Compression at contact, Anchor at a point, and Lira's one-handed shooting as a coordinated solution (54:191–265, 267–323).
+- Violence stays intense but non-lurid. Brom's reopened shoulder, Cael's old ribs, and the living creature's injury are described through function, choice, and treatment; the animal is explicitly left alive (54:139–175, 191–241, 251–303; 55:3–31, 49–107, 153–165).
+- Final body continuity holds. Brom's right shoulder is mended a second time and may not be mended a third this cold term; the non-Path binder adds a four-yard drover's web (55:25–45; 56:33–67). Lira's forearm remains in its high sling and is not released merely because snow falls; ankle remains taped/flat and never mended (58:17–27; 59:23–45, 121–129). Cael's old ribs speak for ten days and clear on day 129 (55:89–103; 59:19–21, 47–49). Oryn's reserve is full after three days without mending, then spends two at Thornwater (60:109–119, 147–175).
+- Consent debt is fully paid without forgiveness. Cael completes three self-readings, tells Oryn first and all at once, and receives a second explicit yes before reading her during the telling (55:169–219, 221–271). Oryn marks that performance debt paid while keeping the original taking where she put it (55:275–287); her later POV says plainly that she has not forgiven him (60:121–125). At Teague's wrist Cael does not read and does not even ask, because curiosity alone is not a purpose and Teague's guarded information is his to offer (56:153–205). This final “wrist not read” makes asking the person whose body it is a lived rule, not just a vow.
+- “The still place” knowledge boundary holds: it is Cael's old private label until he tells Oryn (55:193–203, 243–279), then tells the crew after her (57:191–211). It is explicitly distinguished from the Quieting and never given a cause (55:195–203, 257–279; 60:35–39).
+- Three identical smaller sites establish perimeter, radius, forty-one sign kinds, and the lone radius-divided line; the fourth is paced only from outside, never entered, left unnamed, and is twice the size with a registry cordon (56:3–17; 57:13–23, 57–79, 91–125; 58:117–161, 165–225). The ending's “four sites, one line” is warranted as map alignment, not equivalence of interiors (58:225–229; 60:237–265).
+- Protected maker limit holds: the only final maker sentence is “Someone made this pattern” (60:247–253), supported by four aligned sites but not expanded into who, why, or how. The preceding thought remains an inference, not spoken fact (60:247–251).
+- Names/roles hold: the fourth site receives no name; Teague's people remain bow/spear/boy/old woman; the Hall creature gets only a carter's folklore label in reported speech, not an authoritative naming (53:117–123; 56:19–25, 71–109; 58:125–139).
+- Money closes exactly: 102 remains through the Stair (52:355–359), then six marks purchase the Lowmarch paper room, leaving 96 in hand (60:3–13, 29–31). The 300 remains taken/not paid; no contract money is added (59:161–175).
+- Board/sheets close exactly: Pike records nine lines and leaves the season's rating blank while the wall remains eleventh (59:175–207, 211–217; 60:29–31). Sheets total eleven Ring + twenty-nine Stair + twelve Hall = fifty-two (57:13–17; 60:19–25).
+- Exit lands. The book moves from “nothing out here reads me” to freedom complicated by his unique function, then to an oriented search governed by consent and shared evidence (58:99–113, 219–229; 60:31–43, 247–265). The final sentence stops at the defensible boundary: maker/pattern, not motive. It hands Book 8 a direction, a thaw deadline, Teague's alliance, Oryn's return condition, and an unopened fourth site without relying on Book 8's unreconciled plan (59:219–225; 60:215–265).
+- Repetition watch: “as he/she had...” retrospective comparisons remain very dense and repeatedly pull present action back through prior scenes (54:3–29, 91–107, 159–175; 55:21–29, 61–75, 169–203; 58:95–113; 60:69–83). “A person...” generalizations recur as explanatory codas (55:113–119, 137–151; 56:47–61, 173–181; 60:101–125). Counting, hands, bowls, and “entered/noted” deliberately close motifs but create a highly patterned surface.
