+## Final mechanical audits
+
+- `formula_metrics.py` over all sixty chapters: 306,492 words; 22,130 sentences; mean sentence 13.85, median 10; 8,861 paragraphs, mean 34.59 and median 24; 263 marked breaks; 948.9 words per scene; Flesch 94.0; FK 3.59. Word-count median is 5,029. Ch18 is shortest at 3,452 and ch22 longest at 6,549; ch10 has the highest mean/grade (15.75 / 4.29), ch33 the lowest (12.58 / 2.96). The low grade does not make the prose read infantile; the moral and inferential load remains substantial.
+- Season/unit search found no named season, month name/order, English weekday name, or metric unit. Generic `season`/`month` remain only in allowed uses. `fathom by fathom` at 60:91 is a non-metric rope measure, not a violation.
+- Every one of the 51 non-comment regex units in `protected-patterns.txt` occurs exactly once under the file's normalization rules. Page audit of BOOK_MAP §10 found the mapped documents, letters, logs, exchanges, inventory and closing intact; no protected document is printed twice. Owner-pending #49, #50 and #51 remain verbatim at 27:237–239 / 30:237 / 33:223–273 / 44:219 / 58:229 / 60:255–265, 46:111, and 44:219 respectively.
+- Deployment-line sweep is monotonic and exact: none through 9:317; one from 11:419 through 27:239; thirteen from 33:223 through 46:195; fourteen after the consented Tide read at 48:281; twenty-three after the Stair at 51:217; twenty-six after the Hall at 55:163; twenty-seven after the second consented Tide read at 55:301 and at the close 60:31.
+- Repetition pools (case-insensitive occurrences; lane A ch1–30 / lane B ch31–60): `hand(s)` 1,508 (687/821); count-family 608 (279/329); `that was` 334 (155/179); retrospective `as [subject] had` 315 (125/190); enter-family 112 (36/76); price-family 105 (51/54); cost/bill-family 147 (82/65); `which was` 115 (46/69); `as if/as though` 90 (52/38); `at once` 89 (43/46); measured pause family 89 (42/47); repeated-look family 69 (44/25). Legacy exacts: `squared` 2; `quarter-turn` 0; `for a moment/while` plus `after a while` 11; `did not look` 4; `nobody said` 3; `did not ask` 8; approximate `not X but Y` 19; `He found that` 4. Exact `flat` is 111, mostly terrain, stance, hands or geometry rather than the Book 6 voice tic.
